==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Filibuster Cat Y''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Metafilibuster''' at level 20 using [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]] and XP after completing [[A Whole New World|Zero Field]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Because of his high range, Filibuster Cat X is easily stackable on stages that allow doing so at the beginning; however, it is very difficult to do without proper support, as he has very low health, a long cooldown, and can't fend for himself with his slow attack rate. The [[Freeze]] ability can create a window of opportunity to approach certain dangerous enemies like [[Master A.]], [[Le'boin]], and [[Camelle]], but is ultimately niche. Players are likely to pick up far superior counters long before completing COTC 3, and would have developed adequate strategies to fight them off anyways.

==='''True Form'''===
Metafilibuster gains many stat boosts and abilities, but unless his talents are factored in, should still not be considered as your primary source of offense or crowd-control. Despite his improved attack rate and damage, his attack animation remains extremely long, making him prone to missing attacks. While the ability to target Relics may seem useful on paper, by the time you unlock this True Form, you will already have access to far better alternatives. Although, [[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]] is actually useful against [[Kappy Jr.]], [[Kappy Kawano]] and [[Ancient Magamojoe]], but you still need to give him special protection to use him against these enemies.

He finds little applicability against most Relics and Traitless foes thanks in part to his superior rivals, i.e. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]], [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando Jr.]] However, using him alongside powerful rushers, like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]], as well as the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] can yield fruitful results against powerful pushers/backliners like [[M. Ost]]/[[Lowkey]] if timed properly after Metafilibuster's attacks.

==='''Talents'''===
Metafilibuster's Talents breathe new life into this unit, turning him into a viable backliner, even though the unlock requirement is too late in progression to be of much use.

Regardless, the highest priority Talents are '''[[Massive Damage]]''' and '''Attack Buff''' that significantly improve their horrible offense, especially considering he gets a large 80% bonus from Attack Buff instead of the usual 20%. At level 50, his effective damage versus his targets shoots up to a massive ''291,600'', which is very impressive considering his range. As long as targets can be kept inside his reach, he can greatly cripple if not outright eliminate them on his own given enough time.

The '''Freeze Duration Up''' Talent is furthermore a phenomenal boost to his previously lackluster crowd-controlling capabilities, bringing the uptime of the ability to 47% (7 seconds). This sort of ability upgrade synergizes very well with rushers such as Awakened Bahamut Cat and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] against vulnerable units, allowing them to remove helpless threats with little worry of retaliation if he didn't manage to finish the job.

'''Recover Speed Up''' just makes it easier to get him back on the field if he bites the dust prematurely. At 20 seconds, it brings his recharge rate down closer to the standard for many [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] super-backliners such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aphrodite]] and [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]] (110s - 130s range).

Finally, '''Defense Buff''' is pointless. Metafilibuster retains his singular knockback even with the increase in health provided by this Talent; if anything reaches him, he wasn't long for this world anyways. While this may seem to grant applications against enemies that outrange him or help to tank an occasional piercing attack, it's better to resort to other alternatives instead.

==='''Orb'''===
The only Talent Orb worth using is a Relic Massive Damage Orb, allowing Metafilibuster to deal up to ''340,200'' damage to Relic enemies at level 50.

